/-!
# The native trio calculation for H.15.6

For every native trio, `source_lemma_H_15_6` proves the chief flag
0 < V₃ < V₉ < V in the eleven-dimensional cocode, with dimensions three
and nine. The terms are the intrinsic two-core fixed space and the geometric
pair space. Both the two-core and the intrinsic solvable residual generate
V₉ by displacements. The stabilizer induces the full general linear groups
on V₃ and V/V₉, and its actual quotient by the two-core is L₃(2) × S₃.
The native first-moment map, transported by an actual M24 element, identifies
V₉/V₃ equivariantly with the tensor product of the natural factor modules.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, H.15.6,
printed p.401 (PDF p.412), using H.14.1(3), printed p.396. The printed
middle section V₉/V is corrected to V₉/V₃, as required by the strict flag.
-/
